WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:18.352
In December, the snow lay so deep on the mountain that Peter's hut was buried up to the windowsills.

2
00:00:18.353 --> 00:00:20.917
Grandfather's hut was equally buried.

3
00:00:20.918 --> 00:00:31.687
But he had kept his promise to the pastor, and in the fall, at the first sign of snow, he had taken Heidi and the goats down to the village.

4
00:00:31.688 --> 00:00:38.767
For many years, a large house that belonged to a wealthy soldier had stood empty and uncared for.

5
00:00:38.768 --> 00:00:44.887
There were great cracks in the walls, and in winter, icy winds blew right through.

6
00:00:44.888 --> 00:00:52.383
Behind the house stood a tall ruined chapel with two collapsed walls and only half a roof.

7
00:00:52.384 --> 00:00:58.177
When Grandfather had made up his mind to spend the winter in Dorfli, he had rented the old house.

8
00:00:58.178 --> 00:01:05.431
Being handy with tools, he had known that he could make it livable again and had worked on it during the autumn.

9
00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:10.294
In the middle of October, he and Heidi went to live there.

10
00:01:10.295 --> 00:01:19.043
Grandfather had cleaned out the ruined chapel and, with a few planks of wood, made it into a pen for his goats.

11
00:01:19.044 --> 00:01:26.536
In the house, he led Heidi into a small room with a solid oak door where he had set up his bed.

12
00:01:26.537 --> 00:01:30.771
Through a second door, she could see a huge kitchen.

13
00:01:30.772 --> 00:01:36.456
They walked through it, and on the other side was a fine room in good condition.

14
00:01:36.457 --> 00:01:42.765
In the corner, an enormous stove with painted tiles reached almost to the ceiling.

15
00:01:42.766 --> 00:01:52.154
Heidi ran straight over and, as she looked at its pretty tiles, she discovered her bed in the space behind it.

16
00:01:52.155 --> 00:02:03.403
Grandfather had brought her bed from the loft and set it up, with its mattress of hay tucked under a sheet and her warm blanket on top.

17
00:02:03.404 --> 00:02:10.039
"Oh, Grandfather," Heidi exclaimed. "Is this my room? It's lovely."

18
00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:19.160
Grandfather had patched all the walls and there was still much to do, but Heidi liked their new home very much.

19
00:02:19.161 --> 00:02:24.626
During the winter, Heidi went to school and enjoyed learning with the other children.

20
00:02:24.627 --> 00:02:32.936
Peter went to school whenever the mountain path was clear and would always visit with Heidi and Grandfather on his way home.

21
00:02:32.937 --> 00:02:40.899
Heidi had paid the baker for Grannie's daily rolls, and Peter dutifully picked them up whenever he came to town.

22
00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:48.224
One day, Grandfather decided the weather was nice enough for Heidi to go with Peter up to visit Grannie.

23
00:02:48.225 --> 00:02:53.746
When Peter led her into the hut, Grannie wasn't in her usual chair in the corner.

24
00:02:53.747 --> 00:02:56.884
"Grannie's in bed," Peter explained.

25
00:02:56.885 --> 00:03:01.272
"She isn't very well, and feels the cold badly."

26
00:03:01.273 --> 00:03:06.663
Heidi stepped into the next room where the old woman lay on her narrow bed.

27
00:03:06.664 --> 00:03:08.987
"Are you very ill, Grannie?"

28
00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:11.902
asked Heidi, standing close beside her.

29
00:03:11.903 --> 00:03:16.566
"No, no," she said, reaching out to touch Heidi.

30
00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:20.499
"It's only the frost in my old bones.

31
00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:29.719
I really meant to get up today─this bed is so hard─but I'll be all right again tomorrow."

32
00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:35.013
"I wish I could have brought the big bed I had in Frankfurt," Heidi said.

33
00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:40.255
"It had three fat pillows and was as soft as feathers."

34
00:03:40.256 --> 00:03:47.072
"That would be very cozy, indeed," said Grannie with a sigh.

35
00:03:47.073 --> 00:03:55.772
"But I have so much to be thankful for, the lovely rolls every day and the coffee to drink with them.

36
00:03:55.773 --> 00:03:59.278
And now, you to visit me."

37
00:03:59.279 --> 00:04:04.322
Heidi fetched the familiar prayer book and sat on the edge of the bed to read.

38
00:04:04.323 --> 00:04:14.597
Grannie smiled happily, but Heidi decided to pray that night for a softer bed for Grannie to rest in.
